It is late morning.
I take my backpack and go outside.
I walk to a large flea market in a park.
On Berlin Sundays, there is always a lot going on at the flea markets.
I often come here.
Sometimes I buy a little something.
But mostly I just look.
I walk slowly between the tables.
The sun is shining and the mood is good.
At one stall I see beautiful clothes.
A vendor stands behind the table.
He notices my look and takes a brown jacket.
"Are you looking for a jacket?" he asks me.
"That jacket there is very beautiful," he says.
I politely shake my head.
"No thank you, I do not want that jacket," I answer.
I point to another jacket on the table.
"But I would like to look at this jacket here," I say.
The vendor smiles.
"Of course, here you go," he says and gives me the blue jacket.
